# AirMouse indoor flight settings - always used in the maze (with or without GPS).

# Fly on the REAL navigation filter (EKF3), like the physical flight controller.
# SITL otherwise defaults to AHRS_EKF_TYPE 10 = "cheat with simulator ground truth", which
# silently ignored SLAM (found 2026-09-18: targets came out rotated 90 deg).
AHRS_EKF_TYPE 3

# Cruise speed. Was 0.5 m/s / 1.0 m/s^2 (slow and gentle, "SLAM and the camera need this"): that made travel
# the biggest chunk of a mission (2026-09-18: ~60 m flown at 0.5 m/s = 120 s of a 159 s flight) and SLAM
# tracked to 0.03 m at that speed in rooms. 1.0 m/s is the first step up; go higher only after a flight
# shows SLAM error and wall clearance still hold. The survivor camera (not built yet) may want a lower
# speed while it looks - set it per phase then.
# (ArduPilot 4.7+ renamed WPNAV_SPEED etc. to WP_SPD etc. and switched to m/s)
WP_SPD 1.0
WP_ACC 2.0
WP_SPD_UP 1.0
WP_SPD_DN 0.5

# Landing. ArduPilot waits DISARM_DELAY (default 10 s!) after touchdown before disarming - that was most of a
# 16 s landing from 1.2 m. LAND_SPD_HIGH_MS is the descent speed above the final stage (0 = use WP_SPD_DN);
# the last stage keeps the gentle LAND_SPD_MS default of 0.5 m/s.
DISARM_DELAY 3
LAND_SPD_HIGH_MS 1.0

# The sim drone weighs 1.3 kg (our real drone) but keeps the Iris motors, so it hovers well below the Iris's
# 0.39. Start near it; ArduPilot learns the real value in flight (MOT_HOVER_LEARN).
MOT_THST_HOVER 0.28

# Flying on VELOCITY setpoints (explorer control:=velocity): keep the nose where we point it. The default
# behaviour turns the drone to face the direction of travel, which would spin the 200 deg side cameras around
# and invalidate the LiDAR sector the wall guard is watching.
WP_YAW_BEHAVIOR 0
